Q1. Import a CSV file of Zomato restaurant listings into Power BI and use the 'Split Column by Delimiter' feature to separate the 'Restaurant Name - Area' column into two columns: 'Restaurant Name' and 'Area'.
Ans:- Steps:
Open Power BI Desktop.
Go to Home → Get Data → Text/CSV.
Select the Zomato restaurant CSV file.
Click Transform Data to open Power Query Editor.
Select the Restaurant Name - Area column.
Go to Transform → Split Column → By Delimiter.
Select the delimiter used between the restaurant name and area, such as " - ".
Select Split at the left-most delimiter if appropriate.
Click OK.
Rename the resulting columns:
First column → Restaurant Name
Second column → Area

Q2. Use the 'Merge Columns' feature in Power BI to combine 'First Name' and 'Last Name' columns from a Flipkart user data table into a single 'Full Name' column, separated by a space.
Ans:- Steps:
Open the Flipkart user table in Power Query Editor.
Select the First Name column.
Hold Ctrl and select Last Name.
Go to Transform → Merge Columns.
Select Space as the separator.
Enter the new column name:
Full Name
Click OK.

Q3. Replace all instances of the value 'Cancelled' with 'Order Failed' in the 'Order Status' column of a Swiggy orders dataset using Power BI's 'Replace Values' function.
Ans:- Steps:
Open the Swiggy orders table in Power Query Editor.
Select the Order Status column.
Go to Transform → Replace Values.
In Value To Find, enter:

Cancelled
In Replace With, enter:

Order Failed
Click OK.

Q4. Change the data type of the 'Order Amount' column from Text to Decimal Number in a Paytm transaction table in Power BI, and verify that the column now supports numerical calculations.
Ans:- Steps:
Open the Paytm transaction table in Power Query Editor.
Select the Order Amount column.
Click the Data Type icon on the column header.
Select Decimal Number.
If Power BI asks for confirmation, select Replace Current.

Q5. In a Movie Ticket Booking dataset (like BookMyShow), use the 'Fill Down' operation in Power BI to fill missing 'Movie Name' values based on the previous row's value
.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Blank rows for 'Movie Name' should inherit the name from the last non-blank entry above.</em>
Ans:- Steps:
Open the Movie Ticket Booking dataset in Power Query Editor.
Select the Movie Name column.
Go to Transform → Fill → Down.
Power Query will fill the blank values with the previous non-blank value.
